[ser@sactoh0.UUCP (Shawn E. Riggins) writes:]
[] Once I lucked out and got a wand of wishing, and I used one of my
[] wishes for a scroll of charging.  By doing this I managed to
[] squeeze 3 more wishes out of my wand.  I tried to repeat this but

some will agree that is quite clever. however, in my limited survey
conducted awhile back no one was in favor of getting 7 wishes at
one time. getting 3 wishes seemed like a "natural" number. 7 wishes
at once sounds like moria/omega, oops, i meant sounds wrong. there
was also a significant sentiment for getting wishes distributed
more evenly in time so that, in effect, you could get > 7 wishes
in a game if that game lasted long enough.

now, why is it that a wand of wishing doesn't seem to fit the
expectation of a wand? it would seem that a wand of wishing, if such
a thing were to exist, would be a unique item (perhaps sequestered
somewhere uniquely) and not a generic, but rare item.

hopefully future versions of the game will clean up the subtle flaw
in nethack which relies on a player's ignorance as part of the play
of the game. this would affect various things such as wands of
wishing and dragon scale mail. just my 2 zorkmids worth ...

